### Component 3: SSH Crontab Discovery & Precise Grep Matching

#### [MODIFY] [CrontabExtractor.java](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/service/CrontabExtractor.java)
- Connect via SSH using `config.getSshPort()`.
- Execute `crontab -l`.
- Parse lines into `CrontabJob` (command, schedule, raw line).
- Filter out comments and blank lines.

#### [MODIFY] [CrontabJobMatcher.java](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/service/CrontabJobMatcher.java)
- Match against both `socketPort` and `configName`:
  - `socketPort`: Matches with word-boundary or option prefix (e.g., `-p\s*60170` or `\b60170\b`).
  - `configName`: Matches substring or option prefix (e.g., `-c\s*CPYQSP` or `CPYQSP`).
- If multiple lines match, pick the most specific match or log candidates.
- Extract the exact executable command line from the crontab line (stripping the schedule fields).

---

### Component 4: Trigger Service with Rerun Scheduling

#### [MODIFY] [EtlSshTriggerService.java](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/service/EtlSshTriggerService.java)
- Add method: `discoverCrontabSetup(PipelineConfig pipeline)`:
  - Looks up ETL server from `pipeline.server()`.
  - SSHs to server, runs `crontab -l`, finds matching command using `pipeline.socketPort()` and `pipeline.configName()`.
  - Returns discovered cron info (cron schedule, command, full line).
- Add method: `triggerPipeline(PipelineConfig pipeline, String sessionId, Integer rerunPeriodMinutesOverride)`:
  - Discovers crontab command (or uses cached).
  - Executes the command over SSH.
  - If `rerunPeriodMinutes > 0`: Schedules an asynchronous rerun task via `ScheduledExecutorService` with the specified delay.
  - Records trigger result, execution timestamp, and scheduled rerun info in session metadata.

#### [MODIFY] [EtlTriggerProperties.java](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/config/EtlTriggerProperties.java)
- Add rerun executor thread pool configuration (`rerunPoolSize: 4`).
- Add `dryRun: false` support (allows logging what would run without executing SSH command).

---

### Component 5: Pipeline Orchestrator Integration & Stage Progress Tracking

#### [MODIFY] [PipelineOrchestrator.java](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/pipeline/PipelineOrchestrator.java)
- Associate stage records and session states with the active `PipelineConfig`.
- When CP stage is evaluated:
  - Check whether initial ETL trigger succeeded.
  - Track if a rerun is scheduled or pending.
  - Feed into `CpCompletionHandler` for ES log detection.
- Advance stages upon completion (`CP` $\rightarrow$ `PPLOG` $\rightarrow$ `EXENSIO` $\rightarrow$ `DONE`).

#### [MODIFY] [StageSessionService.java](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/service/StageSessionService.java)
- When a reload session is created:
  - Resolve the pipeline for the given site/job.
  - Call `etlSshTriggerService.triggerPipeline()`.
  - Store trigger status, discovered crontab command, and rerun status in session record.

---

### Component 6: Dashboard & Diagnostic Endpoints

#### [MODIFY] [EtlTriggerController.java](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/controller/EtlTriggerController.java)
- `GET /api/etl-trigger/discover?pipelineKey=...`:
  - SSH to server and return the matched crontab command without executing.
- `POST /api/etl-trigger/trigger`:
  - Triggers the pipeline crontab command with optional rerun delay override.

#### [MODIFY] [DashboardController.java](file:///c:/Users/fg8n8x/Desktop/wip/exensioreload/backend/src/main/java/com/onsemi/cim/apps/exensio/exensioreload/controller/DashboardController.java)
- Add pipeline overview to dashboard snapshot:
  - List configured pipelines with their site, server, socketPort, configName.
  - Current stage distribution per pipeline (`CP`, `PPLOG`, `EXENSIO`, `DONE`).
  - Active triggers and pending reruns.

